<title>USA: Chromcraft acquires Cochrane Furniture.</title>
<headline>Chromcraft acquires Cochrane Furniture.</headline>
<dateline>DELPHI, Ind. 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chromcraft Revington Inc said it acquired Cochrane Furniture Co Inc for about $27 million, including debt assumption.</p>
<p>Outstanding shares of common stock of Cochrane were converted into rights to receive cash payments of $4.75 per share, Chromcraft said.</p>
<p>Cochrane, which makes and sells dining room, bedroom and upholstered furniture, will become a unit of Chromcraft Revington, based in Delphi. Cochrane had sales of $86 million for the fiscal year ended March 30, 1996.</p>
<p>Chromcraft, with sales of $153 million for the year ended December 31, 1995, designs, makes and sells dining and commercial furniture.</p>
<p>--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787</p>
